## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of low-level synchronization, atomic primitives, and memory ordering in a beginner-friendly way.

## Key Concepts
- atomic_flag basics
- memory_order_acquire/release semantics
- backoff to avoid livelock
- cache-line padding to prevent false sharing

## Code Example
```c
#include <stdatomic.h>

typedef struct { 
    alignas(64) atomic_flag flag; 
} spinlock_t;

void spinlock_init(spinlock_t* s) {
    atomic_flag_clear(&s->flag);
}

void spinlock_lock(spinlock_t* s) {
    while (atomic_flag_test_and_set_explicit(&s->flag, memory_order_acquire)) {
        // Simple backoff to prevent livelock
        for (volatile int i = 0; i < 100; i++);
    }
}

void spinlock_unlock(spinlock_t* s) {
    atomic_flag_clear_explicit(&s->flag, memory_order_release);
}

bool spinlock_trylock(spinlock_t* s) {
    return !atomic_flag_test_and_set_explicit(&s->flag, memory_order_acquire);
}
```

## Stress Test
```c
#include <pthread.h>
#include <stdio.h>

spinlock_t lock;
long long counter = 0;

void* thread_func(void* arg) {
    for (int i = 0; i < 1000000; i++) {
        spinlock_lock(&lock);
        counter++;
        spinlock_unlock(&lock);
    }
    return NULL;
}

int main() {
    spinlock_init(&lock);
    pthread_t t1, t2;

    pthread_create(&t1, NULL, thread_func, NULL);
    pthread_create(&t2, NULL, thread_func, NULL);

    pthread_join(t1, NULL);
    pthread_join(t2, NULL);

    printf("Final counter: %lld\n", counter);
    return 0;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical low-level data structure design under bounded resources, including probing, memory layout, and edge handling (empty slots, full table).

## Key Concepts
- Open addressing with linear probing
- Fixed capacity and sentinel handling
- Separate arrays for keys and values for cache locality
- Return conventions for success/failure

## Code Example
```c
#include <stdint.h>
#include <stddef.h>

#define N (1<<12)
static uint32_t keys[N];
static uint64_t vals[N];

static inline size_t probe(uint32_t k) { return k % N; }

void ht_init() {
  for (size_t i = 0; i < N; ++i) keys[i] = 0;
}

int ht_insert(uint32_t k, uint64_t v) {
  if (k == 0) return -1; // sentinel reserved
  size_t idx = probe(k);
  for (size_t i = 0; i < N; ++i) {
    if (keys[idx] == 0) { keys[idx] = k; vals[idx] = v; return 0; }
    if (keys[idx] == k) { vals[idx] = v; return 0; }
    idx = (idx + 1) % N;
  }
  return -1; // full
}

int ht_lookup(uint32_t k, uint64_t* out) {
  if (k == 0) return -1;
  size_t idx = probe(k);
  for (size_t i = 0; i < N; ++i) {
    if (keys[idx] == 0) return -1;
    if (keys[idx] == k) { *out = vals[idx]; return 0; }
    idx = (idx + 1) % N;
  }
  return -1;
}
```

